-- title:
--   Local box of a maximal order is locally maximal
-- statement:
--   Let $a,b\in\mathbb{Q}$ and let $\Lambda_1,\Lambda_2$ be $\mathbb{Z}$-submodules of the quaternion algebra $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]$. Assume $\Lambda_1$ is a maximal order in the sense of the project: it contains $1$, is closed under multiplication, its $\mathbb{Q}$-span is all of $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]$, it is finitely generated over $\mathbb{Z}$, and every submodule $\Lambda'$ with these four properties containing $\Lambda_1$ equals $\Lambda_1$. Let $v$ be a height-one prime of $\mathcal{O}_{\mathbb{Q}}$, let $\varphi$ be a ring isomorphism $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]\otimes_{\mathbb{Q}}\mathbb{Q}_v\cong M_2(\mathbb{Q}_v)$ (where $\mathbb{Q}_v$ denotes the $v$-adic completion) carrying $1\otimes r$ to the scalar matrix $r\cdot 1$, and let $H\in\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{Q}_v)$. Write $\mathrm{localBox}(\Lambda,v)$ for the additive subgroup of $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]\otimes_{\mathbb{Q}}\mathbb{Q}_v$ generated by the elements $z\otimes c$ with $z\in\Lambda$ and $c$ in the $v$-adic integers. Assume $\mathrm{localBox}(\Lambda_2,v)$ consists exactly of those $x$ for which all entries of $H^{-1}\varphi(x)H$ lie in the $v$-adic integers, and assume $\mathrm{localBox}(\Lambda_1,v)\subseteq\mathrm{localBox}(\Lambda_2,v)$. Then $\mathrm{localBox}(\Lambda_1,v)=\mathrm{localBox}(\Lambda_2,v)$. No order hypothesis is imposed on $\Lambda_2$ itself.
--
--   This is the local-maximality consequence of global maximality: a maximal order whose $v$-adic box is contained in a $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{Q}_v)$-conjugate of $M_2(\mathbb{Z}_v)$ fills that conjugate. It is used at the places away from the level when normalising a connecting idele for a pair of maximal (and Eichler) orders, in [`QuaternionAlgebra.exists_conjByFiniteIdele_eq_mem_finiteAdeleBox_smul_inv_mem_of_relIndex_eq`](thm.html#QuaternionAlgebra.exists_conjByFiniteIdele_eq_mem_finiteAdeleBox_smul_inv_mem_of_relIndex_eq).
